--TEST--
A `catch` clause or arm naming a type no `Throwable` can be does not compile, since it never runs. An interface, `object` and a class of the tree compile — `rule:errors/throwable-hierarchy`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Order {}

interface Retryable {}

class Busy extends RuntimeError implements Retryable {}

class Shop {
    public static function run(): int {
        try {
            throw new Busy("busy");
        } catch (Order $order) {
            // Refused: `Order` does not extend `Throwable`.
            return 1;
        } catch (int $number) {
            // Refused: an `int` is never thrown.
            return 2;
        } catch (Retryable $retry) {
            // Accepted: `Busy` implements `Retryable`.
            return 3;
        } catch (RuntimeError $error) {
            return 4;
        }
    }

    public static function arm(): int {
        // Refused: a `string` is never thrown.
        return Shop::run() catch (string $e) => 0;
    }
}
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0864]: `catch` takes a `Throwable`, and `Order` is not one
%A
error[E0864]: `catch` takes a `Throwable`, and `int` is not one
%A
error[E0864]: `catch` takes a `Throwable`, and `string` is not one
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
